<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27509" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δί-στομος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στόμα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>double-mouthed, with two entrances,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέτρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ὁδοί</span>
			<i>double-branching</i> roads, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>OC</u>
				900
			</span></i>; so of rivers <i>with two mouths,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				34.10.5
			</span></i>; <i>with two harbours,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of a weapon,
				<i>two-edged,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξίφος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					983
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πελέκεως γένυς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					530.5
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
